  "summary_en": "US DOT regulation implementing the transportation provisions of Titles II and III of the Americans with Disabilities Act. It sets nondiscrimination duties, accessible vehicle and facility acquisition rules, key station requirements, paratransit and complaint procedures, with appended guidance. It has no AI or robotics provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Entities may not discriminate against individuals with disabilities in transportation service.",
   "Public entities must acquire accessible new vehicles and make key rail stations accessible.",
   "Private entities providing specified public transportation have vehicle acquisition and service duties.",
   "Entities must designate a responsible employee and adopt complaint procedures.",
   "Enforcement via DOT, DOJ, and private right of action."
